<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n51580" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Zōpyrus</span></b> , i,
			m., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ζώπυρος</span>. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>A celebrated physiognomist</i>, <i><span class="en">Cic. Fat. 5,
				10</span></i>; <i><span class="en">id. Tusc. 4, 37,
			80</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>A Persian noble</i>, <i>who mutilated
				himself and thereby helped to conquer Babylon</i>, <i><span class="en">Just. 1,
				10, 15</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>III.</b>
			<i>A rhetorician</i>, <i><span class="en">Quint. 3, 6,
				3</span></i>.—Hence, perh., </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>1.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Zōpyrion</span></b> ,
			Lucil. ap. <i><span class="en">Non. p. 210, 28</span></i>.—
			</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Zōpyriātim</span></b> ,
			adv., <i>in the manner of Zopyrus</i>,
			Lucil. ap. <i><span class="en">Non. p. 455, 17</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
